  "body": "Stacked on #972 (which stacks on #967 and #965). Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n`cargo xtask gate quick` now also maps a source file that a sibling includes with `#[path = \"x.rs\"] mod name;` to `(parent, name)`, the module the compiler sees. This is a union with the file's own name, so it never selects fewer suites. Before, it took the file name as a top-level module. `crates/app/src/posting_index_swing.rs` is `app::posting::index_swing`, and the suites already name it `app::posting (index_swing)` correctly. The plan read it as `app::posting_index_swing`, which no map names, so a change to the index-swing safety law selected no suites.\n\n- New `xtask/src/path_mods.rs` (`included_as`), hooked into `quick::plan`.\n- It covers every `#[path]` file in the tree (posting's nine siblings, stock_sim, drill_reach, ui state, ...) without touching any suite header.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1021-path-included-modules.md`. Fixing the plan rather than renaming the maps, which were right.\n- `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` → 20, because xtask is a process file. A fork needs nothing beyond the normal process sync.\n\n## How tested\n- `cargo test -p xtask`: 44 passed. After review, the pin also asserts that posting_sim still selects wall_column_gouge and contour_arc_sim, posting_suppressed selects rest_across_setups, and posting_plasma selects plasma_gate.\n- Earlier pin text: The new pin is `gate_maps_tests::a_path_included_file_selects_its_parents_submodule_suites`: a change to `posting_index_swing.rs` selects `index_swing`, narrows below all of `app::posting`, and the other posting siblings select suites.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\nNot exercised: #1020's `index_swing_horizontal` suite isn't on this branch. Its map uses the same `app::posting (index_swing)` spelling, so it will be selected the same way.\n\nEffort: low\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #1021\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
